    "summary": "- API keys are stored only as SHA-256 hashes plus `last4`. The full `tly_` token is returned once, by POST `/v1/api-keys` and POST `/v1/invites/accept`, and appears nowhere else.\n- Authentication hashes the presented token. Revoked keys and removed members still get 401. Old snapshots with plain-text tokens still load, and the next snapshot contains no plain-text token. `last_used_at` is written at most once a minute per key.\n- Checked by `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` (all pass), plus new tests for token format, hashing, legacy migration, snapshot contents, the throttle,\n...[truncated]",
